      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "applied frequently to व्रत, see for instance Kâdambarî (Târân. Ed.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "p. 340). In the Departmental Second and Third Books the com-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "pound is explained in a slightly different way (see the Glossaries",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "to those books ad finem). And though the former explanation",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "seems to be closer, the authority of Mallinâtha may be cited for",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "the latter. See under Raghuvans'a XIII., 67 where he says",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "इदं चासिधाराचङ्क्रमणतुल्यतादासिधारव्रतमित्युक्तम्. Râmarshi here says असिधारा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "खड्गधारा तद्वद्दुःशक्यम् and under St. 64 he has असिधारायां खड्गधारायां व्रतं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "दुष्करमित्यर्थः. For various meanings of व्रत see Muir's Texts Vol.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "V., 18, 19 and Müller's Translation of the Ṛigveda I., 225, 231-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "2.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXIX.—ग्रास after कवल means swallowing. The reading",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "दलन for कवल has a parallel in S'ṛingâras'ataka St. 59 (Kâvya-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "sangraha). मानमहताम् = great in self-respect or dignity compare",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "मानिन्.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXX.—सत्त्व = greatness. Comp. अगाधसत्त्व. Raghuvans'a VI.,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "21 and commentary of Mallinâtha on it. Râmarshi renders it by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "चित्त. It means पराक्रम. See Vaijayantî noted at Vâsavadattâ p.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "37. For the idea of the Stanza comp. Bhâminîvilâsa I., 49.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXI.—चरणावपात. Râmarshi renders this by पादप्रसारं करोति.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "The other commentator has चरणानां पतनम्. It seems rather to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "mean falling at [another's] feet. पिण्डद = giver of food. Comp.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "Panchatantra I., 76 and Vîracharita p. 81, (Calc. Ed.) where",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "Mâlyavân is called पिण्डोपजीवी of Râvaṇa. पुंगव comp. the syno-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "nymes वृषभ, ऋषभ, similarly used.—Vasantatilakâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXII.—परिवर्तिनि, revolving, rotating. The allusion is to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the ever-recurring birth and death in this world. पुनरपि जननं पुनरपि",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "मरणं पुनरपि जननीजठरे शयनम् are familiar verses to the same effect.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "(They are ascribed to S'ankarâchârya. See Kâvyasangraha 35).—को",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "वा. The particle वा is idiomatically used in this way in questions",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
